# Secret env vars for stocs-auth, one key name per line.
#
# This is the declared complement of .env.{production,staging}.example: that file holds
# everything that is neither generated nor sensitive, and this holds the names of
# everything that is. Between them they describe the app's whole environment.
#
# Key NAMES are not sensitive, which is why this is committed. The values come from the
# environment when render-spec.sh runs: from GitHub Secrets in CI, or exported by hand
# for a local run.
#
# The point of declaring them is that render-spec.sh fails when one is missing, rather
# than emitting a spec with an empty value. An app deployed with an empty APP_KEY or
# MAIL_PASSWORD fails in ways that are slow to attribute, so it is better to refuse.
#
# Anything listed here is marked `type: SECRET` in the generated spec, so DigitalOcean
# encrypts it at rest and `doctl apps spec get` returns ciphertext rather than the value.
#
# NOT listed, deliberately:
#
#   DB_PASSWORD and the rest of the DB_* set. Those come from ${stocs-main.*} bindings in
#   the spec itself, so they never pass through the repo or GitHub at all.
#
#   ADMIN_1_PASSWORD and friends. The migrate job does not seed, so operator admins are
#   created by a one-off command after a first deploy; see .env.production.example. They
#   need to be in the app environment at that moment, not on every deploy.

APP_KEY
MAIL_PASSWORD
